  "content": {
    "id": "p23-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "For each pair of lines, find the coordinates of the point where the graphs intersect.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5x+y&=7\\\\3x-y&=1\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(1,2)$",
          "worked": "Adding the equations:\n$$\\begin{align*}(5x+y)+(3x-y)&=7+1\\\\8x&=8\\\\x&=1\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $5x+y=7$:\n$$\\begin{align*}5(1)+y&=7\\\\y&=2\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $(1,2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x-3y&=5\\\\4x-3y&=13\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac83,-\\dfrac79\\right)$",
          "worked": "Subtracting the first equation from the second:\n$$\\begin{align*}(4x-3y)-(x-3y)&=13-5\\\\3x&=8\\\\x&=\\frac83\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $x-3y=5$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac83-3y&=5\\\\-3y&=\\frac73\\\\y&=-\\frac79\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $\\left(\\dfrac83,-\\dfrac79\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=3+x\\\\3x-2y&=6\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(12,15)$",
          "worked": "Substituting $y=3+x$:\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-2(3+x)&=6\\\\3x-6-2x&=6\\\\x-6&=6\\\\x&=12\\end{align*}$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=3+12\\\\y&=15\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $(12,15)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}y&=2x-10\\\\y&=-3x+4\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(\\dfrac{14}{5},-\\dfrac{22}{5}\\right)$",
          "worked": "Equating the expressions for $y$:\n$$\\begin{align*}2x-10&=-3x+4\\\\5x&=14\\\\x&=\\frac{14}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nThen\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=2\\left(\\frac{14}{5}\\right)-10\\\\y&=\\frac{28}{5}-\\frac{50}{5}\\\\y&=-\\frac{22}{5}\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $\\left(\\dfrac{14}{5},-\\dfrac{22}{5}\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 64
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}x-3y&=13\\\\4x-5y&=18\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(-\\dfrac{11}{7},-\\dfrac{34}{7}\\right)$",
          "worked": "Multiplying the first equation by $4$:\n$$4x-12y=52.$$\nSubtracting this from the second equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}(4x-5y)-(4x-12y)&=18-52\\\\7y&=-34\\\\y&=-\\frac{34}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $x-3y=13$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x-3\\left(-\\frac{34}{7}\\right)&=13\\\\x+\\frac{102}{7}&=\\frac{91}{7}\\\\x&=-\\frac{11}{7}\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $\\left(-\\dfrac{11}{7},-\\dfrac{34}{7}\\right)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 80
      },
      {
        "id": "p23-q10-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "$$\\begin{aligned}5x+y&=8\\\\2x-3y&=10\\end{aligned}$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$(2,-2)$",
          "worked": "Multiplying the first equation by $3$:\n$$15x+3y=24.$$\nAdding this to the second equation:\n$$\\begin{align*}(15x+3y)+(2x-3y)&=24+10\\\\17x&=34\\\\x&=2\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting into $5x+y=8$:\n$$\\begin{align*}5(2)+y&=8\\\\y&=-2\\end{align*}$$\nThe intersection is $(2,-2)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 56
      }
    ]
